<mxCell id="soc" value="GENERATED BY add_milan_datapath() - the sys / cd_milan boundary
AXIS stream CDC  mac_tx_cdc  -  out of the datapath
AXIS stream CDC  mac_rx_cdc  -  into the datapath
AXIS stream CDC  dma_tx_cdc  -  into the datapath
AXIS stream CDC  dma_rx_cdc  -  out of the datapath
AXIS stream CDC  dma_ts_cdc  -  out of the datapath
AXIS stream CDC  dma_pcm_cdc  -  out of the datapath
AXI-Lite CDC  milan_axil_cdc  -  the whole CSR register ABI, sys to cd_milan
MultiReg 2-FF  x5 call sites  -  single-bit status/IRQ levels (incl. the CSR IRQ to sys)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ECEFF1;strokeColor=#455A64;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="630" width="1342" height="172" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="claim" value="What this census can and cannot prove: it proves every crossing built from one of the four primitives is drawn here. It CANNOT prove a signal is not crossing some other way - a bare assignment between two clocked processes is invisible to this parse and to simulation alike. That is what the constraints and the synthesis CDC report are for." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFEBEE;strokeColor=#C62828;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="814" width="1342" height="92" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>